// Resilience without I/O: circuit breaking, rate limiting, adaptive load shedding,
// backoff, rolling windows and deadlines.
//
// Every decision is a function of what the caller passes in. The clock is read by
// the caller (nanoseconds, as in moonpool) and so is the randomness a breaker's
// roll or backoff's jitter needs, which is what makes every sequence here
// reproducible in a test. Policy numbers are parameters whose presets are the
// values go-zero ships.
//
// The jitter strategies are the ones AWS's "Exponential Backoff and Jitter"
// (https://aws.amazon.com/builders-library/timeouts-retries-and-backoff-with-jitter/)
// names and measures.
import {
  "moonbitstack/moondate",
}
